# mdwfDiracModes: low eigenmodes of the MDWF kernel (spectrum = kernel: H_W^2) or of the 4D effective MDWF Dirac
# operator (spectrum = dirac: D(m)^dagger D(m)), with per-mode IPR, chirality and Ginsparg-Wilson defect 1 - eps^2.
#   Gaugefile          NERSC configuration (required; the example uses the 8^3 x 4 test configuration of the
#                      repository, git lfs pull)
#   smearing           none | fat7_su3 | fat7_u3 (kernel links), smear_steps
#   M5, b5, c_sw, ls   Mobius kernel (c5 = b5 - 1), Ls = 8 or 16; mass = m of D(m) (dirac)
#   nev, nbasis, nkeep thick-restart Lanczos: wanted modes, basis size, kept Ritz vectors (nev <= nkeep < nbasis - 1)
#   cheb_degree        0: plain Lanczos on A; d > 0: on -T_d((hi + lo - 2A)/(hi - lo)), cheb_lo above the wanted
#                      eigenvalues, cheb_hi <= 0: automatic (kernel: 1.05 x plain-Lanczos lambda_max; dirac: 1.02)
#   gw_defect          1: compute <y|1 - eps^2|y> per mode (one Pauli-Villars solve each)
#   pv_precision       Pauli-Villars solves inside D(m); mixed_precision = 1: mixed-precision solver
Lattice          = 8 8 8 4
Nodes            = 1 1 1 1
spectrum         = kernel
smearing         = none
smear_steps      = 2
M5               = 1.8
b5               = 1.5
c_sw             = 0.0
ls               = 8
mass             = 0.0
antiperiodic_t   = 1
nev              = 10
nbasis           = 40
nkeep            = 20
tol              = 1e-8
max_restarts     = 500
cheb_degree      = 0
cheb_lo          = 0.0
cheb_hi          = 0.0
gw_defect        = 1
mixed_precision  = 0
pv_precision     = 1e-11
measurements_dir = ./
output_name      = mdwfDiracModes.dat
Gaugefile        = ../test_conf/nersc.l8t4b3360_bieHB
